 > tiles; I've tried adding OPTIONS=!tiled_map to my .nethackrc file to
 > no avail.

      The X11 interface uses X resources to control the display.
The way things are currently implemented, once nethack parses
its own options stuff it's too late to change; that tiled_map
option only works for MSDOS and/or Qt.

      For X11, you specify tiles or special font or ordinary font
in ~/.Xdefaults or X-application-defaults/NetHack (I don't know
the right path to use here).  The template application defaults
file included with the source distribution, win/X11/NetHack.ad,
contains comments indicating what some of the most significant
entries are for; I don't think they're documented anywhere else.
Ordinary text is the default, so you already have something set
up that is forcing tiles instead (maybe put into place by your
linux packager depending upon how you got nethack going in the
first place...).

